:: Day1_SQ_Ali [day1 sidequest neighborhood ali]
<<nobr>>
<<centerImage "image/location/park.png">>

<p>The bell dings when I walk in and Ali looks up from his crossword and nods. Ali is fifty-three, Pakistani, has run this corner store for eighteen years, and knows every person in a six-block radius by first name, preferred snack, and approximate credit rating. He's short, round, has a mustache that could be described as "ambitious," and does the crossword puzzle from the newspaper every single day in pen because he says pencils are "for cowards."</p>

<<dialog "Alex" "Hey Ali.">>

<p><strong>"Alex! My favorite customer."</strong> He says this to everyone. I've heard him say it to at least nine different people. It doesn't matter. It still works.</p>

<p>His store is a time capsule. The same fluorescent lights buzzing the same frequency since 2006. The same spinning rack of paperbacks. The same hand-written sign above the register that says "SMILE! You are on camera :)" with a smiley face drawn in marker that has faded to the color of a bruise.</p>

<p>I buy a Gatorade. He rings me up without looking at the register because he has every price memorized.</p>

<p><strong>"One seventy-five. How's your mother? The stepmother, I mean."</strong></p>

<p>"She's fine. Same as always."</p>

<p><strong>"Good woman. Scary woman. But good."</strong> He hands me my change. <strong>"And the pink-haired one? Your sister?"</strong></p>

<p>"Step-sister. She's Lily. She's fine too."</p>

<p><strong>"She came in yesterday. Bought three energy drinks and a bag of those sour gummy worms. I told her that much sugar will kill her. She told me she's already dead inside."</strong> He chuckles. <strong>"Funny girl. Scary, but funny."</strong></p>

<p>But today he's just the corner store guy, and I'm just the kid buying Gatorade.</p>

<<set $aliMet to true>>
<<set $aliFamiliarity to 1>>
<<set $money -= 2>>
<<spendTime 1>>
<<set $currentMapLocation to "neighborhood">>

