:: Day1_SQ_Delgado [day1 sidequest park delgado]
<<nobr>>
<<centerImage "image/location/park.png">>

<p>She's ancient. That's the only word for it. Mrs. Delgado is somewhere between eighty and geological time. She sits on the same park bench every afternoon, rain or shine, feeding pigeons from a paper bag full of stale bread that she probably baked during the Cold War.</p>

<p>She watches me with eyes that are milky around the edges but sharp in the center, like old windows in a new frame.</p>

<p><strong>"You're that boy from the Chambers house,"</strong> she says. Not a question. A statement.</p>

<p>"Yes ma'am."</p>

<p><strong>"Your stepmother's got good taste."</strong> She tosses a chunk of bread and three pigeons almost kill each other for it. <strong>"In furniture. In clothes. In how she keeps that house."</strong> A pause. Another bread chunk. <strong>"She'll have good taste in how she keeps you too, I imagine."</strong></p>

<p>I have no idea what that means. I smile politely, nod, keep walking. Behind me I hear her chuckle, dry and papery, like someone crumpling tissue paper.</p>

<p>Mrs. Delgado sees everything in this neighborhood. She's been on that bench longer than the bench has been there. She'll notice the change in me before anyone else does. Not because she's looking for it. Because she's always looking at everything.</p>

<<set $delgadoMet to true>>
<<set $delgadoAwareness to 1>>
<<spendTime 1>>
<<set $currentMapLocation to "neighborhood">>

